  "nl_text": "The schemabench_0220 database is a comprehensive schema that includes 14 tables, each representing a different entity or relationship in the hotel industry. The tables are designed to store information about hotels, reservees, rooms, reservations, booking agencies, activities, offers, guests, departments, employees, gyms, equipment, restaurants, and facilities.\nThe Hotel table contains information about individual hotels, including their location, name, rating, and ID number. The Reservee table stores information about individuals who make reservations, including their ID number. The Room table contains information about individual rooms, including their room number, price, hotel ID, view, availability, and room type. The Reservation table stores information about individual reservations, including the board type, start date, duration, paid amount, children number, reservee ID, and room ID. The Booking_Agency table contains information about booking agencies, including their name, location, discount, and reservee ID.\nThe Activities table contains information about various activities that guests can participate in, including their name, date, and price. The Offers table contains information about offers that hotels make to guests, including the hotel ID and activity ID. The Guest table contains information about individual guests, including their SSN, name, reservee ID, gender, date of birth, reservation ID, and participation in activities. The Participates_in table contains information about the activities that guests participate in, including their guest SSN and activity ID.\nThe Department table contains information about departments within hotels, including their ID number, name, and hotel ID. The Employee table contains information about employees, including their ESSN, name, management ESSN, department ID, hotel ID, salary, and participation in activities. The Gym table contains information about gym facilities, including their ID number, hotel ID, name, working hours, and equipment. The Equipment table contains information about the equipment available in gyms, including their facility ID and equipment name.\nThe Restaurant table contains information about restaurants, including their ID number, hotel ID, name, rating, price range, food type, and facilities. The Facility table contains information about facilities, including their ID number and hotel ID.\nOverall, the schemabench_0220 database schema provides a comprehensive and detailed representation of the hotel industry, with tables that are designed to store information about hotels, reservees, rooms, reservations, booking agencies, activities, offers, guests, departments, employees, gyms, equipment, restaurants, and facilities.",
  "gold_question": "Background / Context\n\nThe project involves developing a management system for a hotel chain. This system aims to efficiently handle hotel operations, including reservations, room management, and activities offered by the hotel chain. It integrates functionalities required by both hotel staff and guests, ensuring seamless operations and enhanced customer service.\n\n Objectives\n\n- To automate hotel reservations and room assignments.\n- To provide guests with easy access to hotel services and amenities.\n- To enable hotel staff to manage daily operations efficiently.\n- To streamline the management of hotel activities and facilities.\n\n Stakeholders & Users\n\n- Hotel Managers: Oversee hotel operations and require reports on performance metrics.\n- Receptionists: Handle reservations, check-ins, and guest services.\n- Guests: Book rooms and participate in hotel activities.\n- Booking Agencies: Facilitate reservations through third-party services.\n- Department Staff: Manage specific areas like housekeeping and restaurants.\n- System Administrators: Maintain system integrity and performance.\n\n Functional Descriptions\n\n1. Reservation Management\n   - Guests and booking agencies can make room reservations.\n   - Manage reservation details including check-in/check-out dates, board type, and payment information.\n   \n2. Room Management\n   - Maintain a database of rooms with details on type, availability, and pricing.\n   - Assign rooms automatically or manually based on reservations.\n\n3. Activity Management\n   - Schedule and manage hotel-hosted activities.\n   - Allow guests to book and participate in activities.\n\n4. Guest Management\n   - Track guest details and their participation in hotel activities.\n   - Link guest data to reservations for service personalization.\n\n5. Facility and Department Management\n   - Manage hotel facilities such as gyms and restaurants.\n   - Oversee departmental operations and staffing.\n\n Non-Functional Descriptions\n\n- Scalability: The system should handle multiple hotels and large volumes of data.\n- Security: Ensure secure handling of personal and payment information.\n- Usability: Provide an intuitive interface for both hotel staff and guests.\n- Performance: Optimize for high availability and fast response times during peak operations.",
  "input_json": "/data/SchemaBench/Experiment/schema2text_codellama13b/0220.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0220\nCREATE TABLE `hotel` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `location` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `rating` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `reservee` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `room` (\n  `room_number` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `price` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `hotel_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `view` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `availability` boolean NOT NULL,\n  `room_type` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`room_number`),\n  CONSTRAINT `room_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`hotel_id`) REFERENCES `hotel` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `reservation` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `board_type` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `start_date` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `duration` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `paid_amount` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `children_number` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `reservee_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `room_number` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `reservation_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`reservee_id`) REFERENCES `reservee` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `reservation_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`room_number`) REFERENCES `room` (`room_number`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `booking_agency` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `location` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `discount` decimal(5,2) NOT NULL,\n  `reservee_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `booking_agency_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`reservee_id`) REFERENCES `reservee` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `activities` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `date` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `price` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `offers` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `hotel_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `activity_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `offers_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`hotel_id`) REFERENCES `hotel` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `offers_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`activity_id`) REFERENCES `activities` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `guest` (\n  `ssn` char(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `reservee_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `gender` char(1) NOT NULL,\n  `date_of_birth` date NOT NULL,\n  `reservation_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`ssn`),\n  CONSTRAINT `guest_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`reservee_id`) REFERENCES `reservee` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `guest_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`reservation_id`) REFERENCES `reservation` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `participates_in` (\n  `guest_ssn` char(11) NOT NULL,\n  `activity_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`guest_ssn`, `activity_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `participates_in_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`guest_ssn`) REFERENCES `guest` (`ssn`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `participates_in_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`activity_id`) REFERENCES `activities` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `department` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `hotel_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `department_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`hotel_id`) REFERENCES `hotel` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `employee` (\n  `essn` char(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `management_essn` char(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `department_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `hotel_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `salary` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`essn`),\n  CONSTRAINT `employee_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`department_id`) REFERENCES `department` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `employee_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`hotel_id`) REFERENCES `hotel` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `gym` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `hotel_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `working_hours` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `gym_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`hotel_id`) REFERENCES `hotel` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `equipment` (\n  `facility_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`facility_id`, `name`),\n  CONSTRAINT `equipment_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`facility_id`) REFERENCES `gym` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `restaurant` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `hotel_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `rating` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `price_range` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `food_type` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `restaurant_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`hotel_id`) REFERENCES `hotel` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `facility` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `hotel_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `facility_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`hotel_id`) REFERENCES `hotel` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
